      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The dexamethasone-eluting stent was a well-tolerated and effective means of providing sustained site-specific drug delivery to the porcine coronary artery wall for 28 days, although longer-term biocompatibility of the polymer coating was not assessed. Dexamethasone did not reduce the neointimal hyperplastic response to injury, despite sustained tissue levels of drug."},
